<title>UK: Baltic Freight Index fell one point to 1,279.</title>
<headline>Baltic Freight Index fell one point to 1,279.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Baltic Freight Index for</p>
<p>spot dry cargo shipping rates fell to 1,279 today from</p>
<p>1,280 on Aug 5, with the base being Jan 4 1985 equals</p>
<p>1,000. The BFI is based on the following sub-indices with rates</p>
<p>in dollars per tonne.</p>
<p> Route Index     Rate   Prev Index  Rate</p>
<p>   1    1355    12.300	  1362    12.369</p>
<p>   1a   1252  9481.000	  1256  9513.000</p>
<p>   2    1588    22.688	  1589    22.700</p>
<p>   2a   1504 12338.000	  1508 12369.000</p>
<p>   3    1381    12.744	  1381    12.744</p>
<p>   3a   1157  9131.000	  1152  9094.000</p>
<p>   6    1276    13.163	  1276    13.163</p>
<p>   7    1167     5.681	  1163     5.663</p>
<p>   8     842     9.263	   843     9.269</p>
<p>   9     688  6013.000	   688  6013.000</p>
<p>  10    1142     5.769	  1140     5.756</p>
